<section class="band band--white">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Testing</p>
    <h1>Try Aegis ID in a working application.</h1>
    <p>Each application below exercises a different part of the platform. Open one, complete the assurance step, then approve the challenge in your Aegis ID wallet and review the evidence in the ledger.</p>
  </div>

  <article class="blade-guidance">
    <strong>Before you start</strong>
    <span>Set up your wallet in the Aegis ID mobile app and connect it to an organization. Credentials and challenges are addressed to a connected organization, so an unconnected wallet will not receive them.</span>
  </article>

  <div class="example-app-grid">
    {{#each testingApps}}
      <article class="example-app-card" id="{{id}}">
        <span class="track-label">{{label}}</span>
        <h3>{{title}}</h3>
        <p class="example-app-card__purpose">{{purpose}}</p>
        <p>{{summary}}</p>

        <ul class="example-app-card__tests">
          {{#each tests}}
            <li>{{this}}</li>
          {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <div class="example-app-card__footer">
          <span class="example-app-card__meta">{{meta}}</span>
          <a class="button button--blue example-app-card__cta" href="{{href}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{action}}</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--light">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Where to look afterwards</p>
    <h2>Every test leaves evidence.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="example-app-grid">
    <article class="example-app-card">
      <h3>Wallet events</h3>
      <p>Authentication, consent, approval, and revocation activity for your organization, in the order it happened.</p>
      <div class="example-app-card__footer">
        <span class="example-app-card__meta">Organization dashboard</span>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="example-app-card">
      <h3>App ledger</h3>
      <p>Cross-application records raised by apps such as Business Expenses when they request a wallet signature.</p>
      <div class="example-app-card__footer">
        <span class="example-app-card__meta">Organization dashboard</span>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="example-app-card">
      <h3>Evidence ledger</h3>
      <p>The tamper-evident chain behind those records. Each entry carries the fingerprint of the one before it, so any edit is detectable.</p>
      <div class="example-app-card__footer">
        <span class="example-app-card__meta">Hash-chained</span>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
